{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED for exact head f116097aacda9aee74ccdac0d6d762f9fe900f2f, artifact fda8bc9b261e96583d8e99d86e722ed8978389cd.\n\n1. The artifact is made mergeable by omitting the governing request/promise and resting only on predecessor d97eed89. That severs the Workroom provenance edge and prevents the staleness flare the repository discipline requires; the commit trailer is not a projection edge. Obtain fresh stable authorization, carry it in the implementing commit, and publish the artifact on both that governing basis and the live predecessor.\n\n2. The shipped gap remains open. MaxQueueDepth is enforced only when positive, but the sole production constructor in internal/app/app.go leaves it zero. Every Gitseq resident therefore remains unbounded. Either wire and document a real resident bound, or obtain the original request's allowed ratified narrowing and report this honestly as a kernel capability rather than completed back-pressure.\n\n3. Strengthen the tests before re-review. TestSubmitRefusesAtCapacityBeforeChaining waits forever if the first slot is accidentally refused; bound the initial arrival. The zero-limit test does not demonstrate more than one queued follower and should pin genuinely unbounded/default-compatible behavior. Most importantly, the Rotate test uses MaxRetries=-1, performs no CAS attempt, and classifies invalid configuration as capacity; it does not prove real retry exhaustion. The production mapping of genuine Rotate CAS exhaustion to the same contention class is reasonable, but validate negative limits separately and exercise real contention with a narrow failpoint, or omit that unproven classification change.\n\nArchitecture: kernel admission/bounds only; storage CAS is consumed but unchanged, and no Workroom/application meaning enters the kernel. The architecture contract is preserved. Security: the pre-lock atomic gate is race-safe and leaves signatures, key rotation, and CAS verification intact, but the production path retains the unbounded request/DoS surface. Simplification: do not carry an unreachable internal option; the smallest honest result is a fixed documented resident bound plus this primitive, or a ratified narrowing. Avoid a helper for the two wrapped error lines.\n\nVerification at the exact clean head: focused tests and focused race pass; make vet, make build, make test, full kernel race, and git diff --check pass. Mutation review found the test gaps above.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:fda8bc9b261e96583d8e99d86e722ed8978389cd","head":"f116097aacda9aee74ccdac0d6d762f9fe900f2f","status":"changes-requested","verdict":"changes-requested"}}